WEBVTT

00:02.397 --> 00:06.733
Water, earth,

00:06.818 --> 00:10.112
fire, air...

00:11.239 --> 00:15.284
Long ago, the four nations
lived together in harmony.

00:15.368 --> 00:18.662
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

00:19.706 --> 00:23.625
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

00:23.710 --> 00:25.544
But when the world needed him most,

00:25.628 --> 00:26.920
he vanished.

00:27.338 --> 00:31.133
A hundred years passed, and my brother
and I discovered the new Avatar,

00:31.217 --> 00:32.801
an airbender named Aang.

00:32.885 --> 00:35.178
And although his
airbending skills are great,

00:35.263 --> 00:37.931
he has a lot to learn
before he's ready to save anyone.

00:38.891 --> 00:42.185
But I believe Aang can save the world.

00:54.490 --> 00:58.160
So, travelers,
the next time you think you hear

00:58.244 --> 01:00.579
a strange large bird talking,

01:00.663 --> 01:07.377
take a closer look. It might not be
a giant parrot, but a flying man,

01:08.004 --> 01:12.507
a member of a secret group
of airwalkers who laugh at gravity

01:12.592 --> 01:15.969
and laugh at those
bound to the earth by it.

01:17.930 --> 01:20.015
Aren't airbender stories the best?

01:20.099 --> 01:22.809
Was it realistic?
Is that how it was back then?

01:22.894 --> 01:24.853
I laugh at gravity all the time.

01:24.937 --> 01:27.064
Ha ha! Gravity.

01:27.148 --> 01:28.648
Jingle, jingle.

01:33.738 --> 01:34.988
Sorry.

01:35.073 --> 01:37.032
Aw. Cheapskates.

01:37.116 --> 01:38.909
Hey, thanks for the story.

01:38.993 --> 01:40.702
Tell it to the cap, boy.

01:45.041 --> 01:48.043
Aw. Much obliged, little bat thing.

01:48.127 --> 01:50.420
It means a lot
to hear airbender stories.

01:50.630 --> 01:52.214
It must have been a hundred years ago

01:52.423 --> 01:53.715
your great-grandpa met them.

01:53.800 --> 01:56.134
What are you prattling about, child?

01:56.219 --> 01:58.595
Great-grandpappy
saw the airwalkers last week.

02:07.230 --> 02:09.189
We're almost
to the Northern Air Temple.

02:09.732 --> 02:11.358
This is where
they had the championships

02:11.442 --> 02:12.609
for sky bison polo.

02:13.861 --> 02:16.488
Do you think
we'll really find airbenders?

02:16.572 --> 02:18.657
You want me to be like you
or totally honest?

02:18.741 --> 02:20.200
Are you saying I'm a liar?

02:20.284 --> 02:22.828
I'm saying you're an optimist.
Same thing, basically.

02:23.287 --> 02:25.080
Hey, guys, look at this!

02:34.048 --> 02:35.924
They really are airbenders!

02:37.677 --> 02:38.969
No, they're not.

02:39.053 --> 02:40.137
What do you mean, they're not?

02:40.221 --> 02:41.430
Those guys are flying!

02:41.848 --> 02:43.974
Gliding maybe, but not flying.

02:44.058 --> 02:45.183
You can tell by the way they move

02:45.268 --> 02:48.270
they're not airbending.
Those people have no spirit.

02:54.902 --> 02:57.487
I don't know, Aang.
That kid seemed pretty spirited.

03:09.959 --> 03:12.627
We'd better find some solid ground
before it finds us.

03:16.757 --> 03:18.133
Ha ha!

03:21.220 --> 03:22.554
Go, Teo!

03:22.638 --> 03:25.223
Show that bald kid how it's done!

03:41.032 --> 03:42.866
Hey there. You're pretty good.

03:43.075 --> 03:46.036
Yeah, I know.
But I can do more than fancy gliding.

04:02.094 --> 04:04.304
Wow! I don't think I can do that.

04:04.472 --> 04:05.972
But here's a good one.

04:28.079 --> 04:29.371
What do you think?

04:29.455 --> 04:30.580
It's great.

04:45.972 --> 04:49.391
Hey, you're a real airbender.

04:49.809 --> 04:51.935
You must be the Avatar.

04:52.019 --> 04:55.272
That's amazing!
I've heard stories about you.

04:55.648 --> 04:56.648
Thanks.

04:56.732 --> 04:59.067
Wow! This glider chair is incredible.

04:59.151 --> 05:01.194
If you think this is good,
wait until you see

05:01.279 --> 05:03.446
the other stuff my dad designed.

05:25.052 --> 05:26.636
Wow!

05:26.846 --> 05:28.763
Yeah, my dad is the mastermind

05:28.848 --> 05:30.348
behind this whole place.

05:30.600 --> 05:32.350
Everything is powered by hot air.

05:32.518 --> 05:34.019
It even pumps hot air currents outside

05:34.103 --> 05:35.645
to give us a lift when we're gliding.

05:35.855 --> 05:37.397
This place is unbelievable.

05:37.481 --> 05:39.190
Yeah. It's great, isn't it?

05:39.275 --> 05:41.318
No. Just unbelievable.

05:41.527 --> 05:43.945
Aang used to come here
a long time ago.

05:44.030 --> 05:46.948
I think he's a little shocked
it's so different.

05:47.283 --> 05:48.408
So better!

05:54.040 --> 05:57.000
This is supposed to be
the history of my people.

06:12.099 --> 06:14.976
I'm sure some parts of the temple
are still the same.

06:19.482 --> 06:21.483
It's nice to see at least
one part of the temple

06:21.567 --> 06:22.734
that isn't ruined.

06:33.454 --> 06:35.664
What the doodle? Don't you know enough

06:35.748 --> 06:38.124
to stay away from construction sites?

06:38.209 --> 06:40.502
We have to make room
for the bathhouse.

06:40.586 --> 06:42.087
Do you know what you did?

06:42.296 --> 06:44.339
You just destroyed something sacred

06:44.423 --> 06:46.132
for a stupid bathhouse.

06:46.217 --> 06:48.593
Well, people around here
are starting to stink.

06:48.678 --> 06:50.679
This whole place stinks.

06:50.763 --> 06:51.971
Hyah!

07:00.189 --> 07:03.566
This is a sacred temple.
You can't treat it this way.

07:03.776 --> 07:05.235
I've seen it when the monks were here.

07:05.319 --> 07:06.653
I know what it's supposed to be like.

07:06.737 --> 07:10.281
The monks? But you're 12.

07:10.366 --> 07:13.034
Dad, he's the Avatar.

07:13.119 --> 07:15.161
He used to come here
a hundred years ago.

07:15.246 --> 07:17.997
What are you doing?
Who said you could be here?

07:18.999 --> 07:20.375
Doing here...

07:20.584 --> 07:23.670
A long time ago,
but not a hundred years,

07:23.754 --> 07:26.005
my people became refugees

07:26.090 --> 07:27.966
after a terrible flood.

07:28.050 --> 07:31.469
My infant son, Teo, was badly hurt

07:31.554 --> 07:32.762
and lost his mother.

07:34.432 --> 07:36.474
I needed somewhere to rebuild,

07:36.642 --> 07:38.435
and I stumbled across this place.

07:38.561 --> 07:39.728
Couldn't believe it.

07:39.812 --> 07:43.857
Everywhere pictures of flying people,
but empty.

07:43.941 --> 07:45.150
Nobody home.

07:45.234 --> 07:48.570
Then I came across
these fan-like contraptions.

07:48.654 --> 07:49.821
Our gliders.

07:49.905 --> 07:52.490
Yes, little light flying machines.

07:52.575 --> 07:53.992
They gave me an idea...

07:54.076 --> 07:57.328
Build a new life for my son
in the air.

07:57.413 --> 08:00.331
Then everyone would be
on equal ground,

08:00.416 --> 08:02.208
so to speak.

08:02.585 --> 08:05.962
We're just in the process of
improving upon what's already here.

08:06.046 --> 08:10.216
And after all,
isn't that what nature does?

08:10.301 --> 08:12.093
Nature knows where to stop.

08:12.178 --> 08:13.678
I suppose that's true.

08:13.763 --> 08:19.142
Unfortunately, progress has a way
of getting away from us.

08:19.226 --> 08:20.435
Look at the time!

08:22.938 --> 08:25.690
Come. The pulley system
must be oiled before dark.

08:25.775 --> 08:28.193
Wait. How can you tell the time
from that thing?

08:28.277 --> 08:30.028
The notches all look the same.

08:30.112 --> 08:32.405
The candle will tell us. Watch.

08:34.533 --> 08:36.618
You put spark powder in the candle!

08:36.702 --> 08:40.455
Four flashes. So it's exactly
four hours past midday,

08:40.539 --> 08:42.665
or as I call it, four o'candle.

08:42.750 --> 08:43.792
Ha ha!

08:43.876 --> 08:45.043
If you liked that,

08:45.127 --> 08:48.129
wait till you see
my finger-safe knife sharpener.

08:48.214 --> 08:51.049
It only took me three tries
to get it right.

08:51.801 --> 08:53.718
Aah!

08:53.928 --> 08:55.053
Follow me.

08:55.137 --> 08:57.347
Hey, Aang,
I want to show you something.

08:58.390 --> 08:59.682
I just can't get over it.

08:59.767 --> 09:01.768
There's not a single thing
that's the same.

09:01.852 --> 09:03.353
I don't know about that.

09:03.437 --> 09:04.604
The temple might be different,

09:04.688 --> 09:07.857
but the creatures that live here are
probably direct descendants

09:07.942 --> 09:10.026
of the ones that lived here
a long time ago.

09:10.110 --> 09:13.655
You're right. They're kind of keepers
of the temple's origins.

09:15.032 --> 09:17.116
Besides, there is
one part of the temple

09:17.201 --> 09:18.409
that hasn't changed at all.

09:19.370 --> 09:20.370
Hey...

09:20.538 --> 09:22.580
It's just like the one
in the other air temple.

09:22.665 --> 09:24.499
Only an airbender can open it.

09:24.583 --> 09:26.709
So inside, it's completely untouched.

09:26.794 --> 09:28.127
Just the way the monks left it.

09:28.295 --> 09:31.005
I've always wondered
what it was like in there.

09:31.423 --> 09:32.465
Aang?

09:32.550 --> 09:35.051
I'm sorry.
This is the last part of the temple

09:35.135 --> 09:36.678
that's the same as it was.

09:36.762 --> 09:38.388
I want it to stay that way.

09:38.931 --> 09:41.099
I completely understand.

09:41.183 --> 09:42.851
I just wanted you to know it was here.

09:42.935 --> 09:44.227
Thanks.

09:49.984 --> 09:53.444
These lanterns are terrible.
I can't see.

09:53.988 --> 09:56.364
Why would you
want to use fireflies for light?

09:56.448 --> 09:59.367
Hey! Close that up. They'll get loose.

09:59.451 --> 10:02.871
Fireflies are
a nonflammable light source.

10:09.003 --> 10:11.129
Cover your nose and hold your breath.

10:12.798 --> 10:15.675
Ok. So you brought me
all the way down here

10:15.759 --> 10:16.968
to see an empty room.

10:17.177 --> 10:18.303
Wrong.

10:18.387 --> 10:21.431
It's filled to the brim
with natural gas.

10:21.515 --> 10:23.474
I came across it my first time here.

10:23.559 --> 10:26.477
Unfortunately, I was
carrying a torch at the time.

10:26.562 --> 10:30.398
Nearly blew myself and the whole place
even more sky-high.

10:30.482 --> 10:33.067
I thought my eyebrows
would never grow back.

10:33.152 --> 10:36.738
Anyway, there's a vital problem
that needs solving.

10:36.947 --> 10:40.033
From time to time, we have gas leaks.

10:40.117 --> 10:42.619
And they're nearly impossible to find.

10:42.912 --> 10:45.246
So this place is an explosion
waiting to happen.

10:45.456 --> 10:48.249
Yes. Until I figure out how to locate

10:48.334 --> 10:52.337
something I can't see,
hear, smell, or touch.

10:52.588 --> 10:54.088
The wind will carry you.

10:54.173 --> 10:55.673
It supports something inside you,

10:55.758 --> 10:57.342
something even lighter than air.

10:57.676 --> 11:00.219
And that something
takes over when you fly.

11:01.639 --> 11:02.889
I've changed my mind.

11:02.973 --> 11:05.099
I think I was born
without that something.

11:05.309 --> 11:08.144
Ha! Impossible. Everybody has it.

11:08.270 --> 11:09.354
Spirit.

11:09.521 --> 11:10.730
What?

11:10.814 --> 11:12.565
That's the something
you're talking about.

11:12.650 --> 11:13.942
Yeah. I suppose it is.

11:16.070 --> 11:17.070
Are you ready?

11:17.196 --> 11:19.864
No! Aah!

11:28.082 --> 11:30.166
I can't believe I'm flying!

11:30.250 --> 11:31.876
Just make sure
you keep your mouth closed

11:31.961 --> 11:33.211
so you don't swallow a bug.

11:35.965 --> 11:37.757
Teo was right about the air.

11:37.841 --> 11:39.509
All I had to do was trust it,

11:39.593 --> 11:41.260
let it carry me.

11:41.345 --> 11:43.221
Even though Teo's not an airbender,

11:43.305 --> 11:45.348
he really does have the spirit of one.

11:48.227 --> 11:49.352
I've been thinking.

11:49.436 --> 11:51.688
If you want to see
what's in that room,

11:51.897 --> 11:53.940
I'd be happy to open the door for you.

11:54.274 --> 11:56.109
- Great.
- Wait!

11:56.193 --> 11:57.610
How do I land this thing?

11:58.070 --> 11:59.404
What if I land over in the...

12:00.948 --> 12:03.658
Blech! Bug. bug.

12:03.742 --> 12:05.368
That was a bug.

12:09.832 --> 12:11.791
I said, don't touch anything.

12:13.669 --> 12:14.794
Don't worry.

12:14.878 --> 12:16.295
That experiment is old,

12:16.380 --> 12:19.799
and that egg was just
part of last week's lunch.

12:21.176 --> 12:23.011
Week-old egg smell.

12:23.095 --> 12:24.137
Quick, find that egg.

12:26.473 --> 12:29.225
I can't believe I'm finally
going to see what's inside.

12:42.281 --> 12:44.782
How could something that's so small,
you can't even see it,

12:44.867 --> 12:46.451
make such a big stink?

12:46.535 --> 12:49.287
That's the solution to our problem.

12:49.371 --> 12:52.248
Yeah. If we put a whole mess
of rotten eggs

12:52.458 --> 12:54.167
in the cellar
where the gas seeps up...

12:54.251 --> 12:57.545
The gas will mix
with the smell of rotten eggs.

12:57.629 --> 12:58.921
Then if there's a leak...

12:59.006 --> 13:00.840
You smell rotten eggs.

13:00.924 --> 13:02.633
Then you just follow your nose

13:02.718 --> 13:05.094
to the place where the smell
is coming from...

13:05.179 --> 13:07.430
And plug up the hole
where the gas is escaping.

13:07.514 --> 13:08.681
-You're a genius!
-You're a genius!

13:10.684 --> 13:12.602
Something is wrong. I've got to go.

13:26.533 --> 13:27.950
This is a nightmare.

13:28.577 --> 13:29.952
You don't understand.

13:30.871 --> 13:32.830
You're making weapons
for the Fire Nation.

13:41.423 --> 13:44.008
You make weapons for the Fire Nation?

13:45.844 --> 13:47.887
Explain all this... Now!

13:48.097 --> 13:50.807
It was about a year
after we moved here.

13:51.016 --> 13:54.393
Fire Nation soldiers
found our settlement.

13:54.478 --> 13:57.271
You were too young
to remember this tale.

13:57.481 --> 13:59.107
They were going to destroy everything,

13:59.191 --> 14:00.691
burn it to the ground.

14:00.776 --> 14:04.070
I pleaded with them.
I begged them to spare us.

14:04.154 --> 14:06.030
They asked what I had to offer.

14:06.281 --> 14:08.908
I offered my services.

14:09.159 --> 14:12.537
You must understand.
I did this for you.

14:22.798 --> 14:24.048
When are they coming?

14:24.842 --> 14:27.927
Soon, very soon.

14:28.053 --> 14:30.388
You can't give them more weapons.

14:30.472 --> 14:32.098
If I don't give them what they want,

14:32.182 --> 14:33.891
they will destroy this place.

14:36.395 --> 14:37.770
How can I be proud of you

14:37.855 --> 14:40.565
when your inventions
are being used for murder?

14:41.150 --> 14:42.984
I need some time to think.

14:44.695 --> 14:46.028
You need to leave. Go.

14:46.113 --> 14:47.613
We're not leaving.

14:47.698 --> 14:49.699
Then hide quickly.

14:53.620 --> 14:55.454
You know better
than to keep me waiting.

14:55.539 --> 14:58.207
Give me what you owe us
so I can be on my way.

14:59.668 --> 15:02.503
Well? Is there a problem?

15:03.297 --> 15:05.131
No. Right this way.

15:07.968 --> 15:09.510
The deal is off.

15:09.595 --> 15:10.761
The Avatar.

15:10.846 --> 15:12.722
Aang, don't get involved.

15:12.931 --> 15:14.724
If I don't get what I came for,

15:14.933 --> 15:17.727
the Fire Nation
will burn this place to rubble.

15:17.811 --> 15:19.228
Get out of here.

15:21.064 --> 15:22.732
You're leaving empty-handed.

15:22.816 --> 15:26.402
Then the destruction of this temple
will be on your head.

15:36.580 --> 15:38.497
This is bad, very bad.

15:38.582 --> 15:40.041
Aang, what are we gonna do?

15:40.125 --> 15:42.376
How can we possibly
keep them all away?

15:42.461 --> 15:43.628
I'll tell you how.

15:43.712 --> 15:45.171
We have something they don't...

15:45.255 --> 15:46.547
Air power.

15:46.632 --> 15:48.257
We control the sky.

15:48.342 --> 15:50.509
That's something
the Fire Nation can't do.

15:50.719 --> 15:52.053
We can win.

15:52.179 --> 15:53.304
I want to help.

15:54.765 --> 15:57.016
Good. We'll need it.

15:58.644 --> 16:00.478
We finally got
the war balloon working,

16:00.562 --> 16:01.938
thanks to Sokka.

16:02.147 --> 16:03.522
This boy is a genius.

16:03.732 --> 16:05.316
Thank you. You're a genius.

16:05.525 --> 16:06.734
Thank you.

16:07.110 --> 16:09.445
See, the problem
with the old war balloon was,

16:09.529 --> 16:10.863
you could get it airborne,

16:10.948 --> 16:13.282
but once you did, it just kept going.

16:13.367 --> 16:14.742
You could put a hole in the top,

16:14.826 --> 16:16.744
but then all the hot air would escape.

16:16.828 --> 16:20.831
So the question became,
how do you keep a lid on hot air?

16:20.999 --> 16:22.541
If only we knew.

16:24.628 --> 16:26.671
A lid is actually the answer.

16:26.797 --> 16:29.840
If you control the hot air,
you control the war balloon.

16:30.050 --> 16:32.927
That's actually pretty smart.

16:33.011 --> 16:34.971
Ok. We got four kinds of bombs...

16:35.180 --> 16:37.431
Smoke, slime, fire, and...

16:37.516 --> 16:38.683
Stink.

16:38.767 --> 16:41.269
Never underestimate
the power of stink.

16:48.068 --> 16:49.360
They're coming!

16:49.569 --> 16:50.736
Are we ready?

16:50.821 --> 16:53.239
Yes, but where's Sokka
with the war balloon?

16:53.323 --> 16:55.324
We'll have to start without it.

17:28.108 --> 17:29.108
Ooh!

17:37.617 --> 17:39.035
Take them out of the sky now!

18:02.601 --> 18:03.642
We've got them on the run.

18:03.852 --> 18:05.311
We need more slime.

18:12.486 --> 18:13.569
Aah!

18:44.851 --> 18:46.102
Whoa!

19:24.933 --> 19:26.851
Yaah!

19:39.948 --> 19:41.532
Those things are unstoppable.

19:41.616 --> 19:43.451
I think I know how they work.

19:43.535 --> 19:46.579
I remember my dad tinkering with
a counterbalancing system,

19:46.663 --> 19:48.080
something to do with water.

19:48.290 --> 19:49.582
Works great?

19:49.749 --> 19:52.209
Water? Can you get me close to one?

19:52.294 --> 19:53.294
No problem.

20:34.169 --> 20:35.836
We're out of bombs.

20:35.921 --> 20:39.131
Come on, Sokka.
Where's that war balloon?

20:48.517 --> 20:50.809
Hey, why aren't they shooting at us?

20:50.894 --> 20:52.186
The insignia.

20:52.270 --> 20:54.271
They think we're on their side.

20:54.356 --> 20:56.398
Then I guess
they won't see this coming.

20:56.483 --> 20:58.484
Bombs away.

20:59.486 --> 21:01.529
Hey! Aah!

21:06.159 --> 21:07.952
No. That was the last one.

21:09.538 --> 21:10.829
Wait a second.

21:10.914 --> 21:12.081
You smell that?

21:12.165 --> 21:14.041
Rotten eggs. There.

21:14.251 --> 21:15.876
That's where the gas is escaping.

21:21.841 --> 21:25.177
What are you doing?
That's our fuel source.

21:25.262 --> 21:27.096
It's the only bomb we've got.

21:48.326 --> 21:50.077
Look. They're retreating.

21:50.161 --> 21:51.662
Yeah!

21:51.746 --> 21:52.830
We're going down!

21:53.164 --> 21:55.124
No! Sokka, hold on!

21:56.418 --> 21:57.668
Get ready.

22:12.350 --> 22:13.350
You know what?

22:13.518 --> 22:15.686
I'm really glad
you guys all live here now.

22:15.895 --> 22:18.981
I realized it's like the hermit crab.

22:19.190 --> 22:20.899
Maybe you weren't born here,

22:21.109 --> 22:23.861
but you found this empty shell
and made it your home,

22:23.987 --> 22:25.904
and now you protect each other.

22:25.989 --> 22:28.032
That means a lot coming from you.

22:28.700 --> 22:30.868
Aang, you were right about air power.

22:30.952 --> 22:32.411
As long as we've got the skies,

22:32.495 --> 22:34.371
we'll have the Fire Nation on the run.

22:49.554 --> 22:53.932
This defeat is the gateway
to many victories.
